// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_scene_lcm_factor0.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: engine/level/scene_dsl.emp's `scene()` guard (3) — the Factor0Lock
// VERIFICATION, all six halves: the 2026-08-28 plane-A closure plus the drift arm the
// band-drift parcel added. The variant
// certifies "the leftmost partial column CANNOT EXIST", which is a PER-PLANE claim: the
// sliver appears on a plane exactly when THAT plane's HScroll is off the 16-px V-scroll
// grain, and the two planes' HScroll words are independent sums. Until 2026-08-28 the
// verification scanned `fb`/`dsb` only, so a scene could lock plane B, declare
// Factor0Lock, pass the build, and still lose its leftmost 16 px on plane A.
//
// SEVEN FIXTURES, ONE AUTHORED FIELD APART — the two-fixture differential run six times
// off one control, so every row's poison differs from the passing shape in exactly the
// field its guard reads:
//
//   FIXTURE OK  — a one-layer per-column scene with BOTH planes locked (fa and fb
//                 FACTOR_0), no curve, no deform amplitude on either plane, declaring
//                 Factor0Lock. It must pass ALL FIVE halves. This control is not
//                 decoration: it is the proof that the tightened guard did not make the
//                 variant unclaimable in principle (see the consequence note at the
//                 guard — it IS unclaimable for a side-scrolling scene, because such a
//                 scene's `fa` tracks the camera; this fixture is the fixed-screen shape
//                 that can still claim it).
//   FIXTURE FA  — OK with `fa: FACTOR_1`. Plane A scrolls. THE HOLE THIS PARCEL CLOSED.
//   FIXTURE FB  — OK with `fb: FACTOR_1_2`. Plane B scrolls. The converse of FA, and the
//                 reason it is here: a guard rewritten to look at plane A must not have
//                 stopped looking at plane B. A fixture that fixes its inputs tests one
//                 number, not the rule.
//   FIXTURE CV  — OK plus `curve: SceneCurve.To(FACTOR_1_2)`. Every `fb` is still locked;
//                 the RAMP walks plane-B HScroll away from zero across the layer, which
//                 the `fb` scan alone cannot see (parallax.emp's `.lp_curve` writes a
//                 moving BG word under a constant FG one). Curves are BG-only by design,
//                 so there is no plane-A twin of this case.
//   FIXTURE DSA — OK plus `dsa: 4` over a scene-level `deform_fg:` table. Both base
//                 factors stay locked; deform adds per-line plane-A HScroll on top.
//   FIXTURE DSB — OK plus `dsb: 4` over a scene-level `deform_bg:` table. The plane-B
//                 twin of DSA, and the liveness check for the half that already existed.
//   FIXTURE DR  — OK plus `drift: SceneDrift.Rate(32)`. Every `fb` is still locked; the
//                 accumulator walks plane-B HScroll away from zero EVERY FRAME and keeps
//                 it there, which the `fb` scan cannot see. The same class as CV, in time
//                 instead of in space. Drift is BG-only, so no plane-A twin.
//
// EXPECTED `[Error]` COUNT IS 6 — one per poisoned fixture, none from the control, and
// no fixture trips a second guard (checked against the full ensure list in scene():
// none authors a pad, an anchor, a vsplit, an own() table, or an out-of-range field; DR's
// rate is inside layer()'s own bounds, so it is refused HERE and nowhere else).
// A 7 means the CONTROL stopped passing — the guard over-fires and Factor0Lock is
// unclaimable even for a genuinely locked scene, which would be a real regression, not
// a stricter gate. A 5 or less means one of the six halves went dead, and since all
// six rows share this count they all report it.
//
// EXPECTED FRAGMENTS (one row each in tools/emp_expect_fail.py's CASES, all count 6):
//   "PLANE A is not locked"        <- fixture FA
//   "PLANE B is not locked"        <- fixture FB
//   "RAMPS its plane-B factor"     <- fixture CV
//   "live H-deform on PLANE A"     <- fixture DSA
//   "live H-deform on PLANE B"     <- fixture DSB
//   "but a layer DRIFTS"           <- fixture DR
//
// THE SIX FRAGMENTS ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE, deliberately: all six messages open with
// the same "left_column_mask: Factor0Lock claims" clause, so matching that alone would
// pass against any of them. Each row's fragment quotes the one clause only its own guard
// says — "PLANE A is not locked", "PLANE B is not locked", "RAMPS its plane-B factor",
// "live H-deform on PLANE A", "live H-deform on PLANE B", "but a layer DRIFTS" — each
// verified to occur exactly once in the tree.
//
// THE TABLE LABEL IS 0, the same spelling every scene poison uses (see
// poison_scene_own_caps.emp): the guards discriminate on the VARIANT and the shifts,
// never on the payload, and a real DeformTable_* name would tie this poison to another
// module's emission.
//
// THE GLOB IMPORTS ARE THE AUTHOR'S OWN SPELLING — see README.md ("Why every scene poison globs").
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_scene_lcm_factor0

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

// FIXTURE OK — both planes locked, no curve, no deform. Must pass all five halves.
const POISON_LCM_F0_OK: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_0, fb: FACTOR_0),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Factor0Lock)

// FIXTURE FA — plane A scrolls. The plane the policy could not see until 2026-08-28.
const POISON_LCM_F0_FA: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_0),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Factor0Lock)

// FIXTURE FB — plane B scrolls. The converse: the pre-existing half must still fire.
const POISON_LCM_F0_FB: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_0, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Factor0Lock)

// FIXTURE CV — both base factors locked, but the plane-B factor RAMPS across the layer.
const POISON_LCM_F0_CV: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_0, fb: FACTOR_0,
                    curve: SceneCurve.To(FACTOR_1_2)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Factor0Lock)

// FIXTURE DSA — both base factors locked, live plane-A deform amplitude over an FG table.
const POISON_LCM_F0_DSA: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_0, fb: FACTOR_0, dsa: 4),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    deform_fg: SceneDeform.Shared(0, 1),
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Factor0Lock)

// FIXTURE DSB — the plane-B twin of DSA.
const POISON_LCM_F0_DSB: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_0, fb: FACTOR_0, dsb: 4),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(0, 1),
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Factor0Lock)

// FIXTURE DR — both base factors locked, no curve, no deform, but the layer DRIFTS. The
// scroll source in TIME rather than in space: the accumulator walks plane-B HScroll away
// from zero every frame and keeps it there, which the `fb` scan can no more see than it
// can see the curve. Drift is BG-only for the curve's reason (plane A is hard-locked to
// -Camera_X), so there is no plane-A twin of this case either.
const POISON_LCM_F0_DR: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_0, fb: FACTOR_0,
                    drift: SceneDrift.Rate(32)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer(),
              no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    v_deform: SceneVDeform.Columns(0, 0, 2),
    left_column_mask: SceneLeftColMask.Factor0Lock)

// ---- THE ANTI-VACUITY HALF (must stay green, and is what FORCES elaboration) ----
// An unreferenced top-level `const X = f(..)` is comptime-inert and proves nothing
// (docs/EMP_PITFALLS.md §3). Naming each fixture's own field here is what makes sigil
// elaborate its `scene()` call, which is what fires the guards above. The predicate is
// the one `lcm_f0` itself tests: a fixture that stopped declaring Factor0Lock would
// silence every guard in the block while still building "clean", and this is what says
// so instead.
ensure(scene_lcm_is_factor0_lock(POISON_LCM_F0_OK.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_factor0: the CONTROL no longer declares Factor0Lock — it stopped being the passing shape the five poisons are differenced against")
ensure(scene_lcm_is_factor0_lock(POISON_LCM_F0_FA.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_factor0: fixture FA no longer declares Factor0Lock — the plane-A lock guard cannot fire on it and its row would prove nothing")
ensure(scene_lcm_is_factor0_lock(POISON_LCM_F0_FB.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_factor0: fixture FB no longer declares Factor0Lock — the plane-B lock guard cannot fire on it and its row would prove nothing")
ensure(scene_lcm_is_factor0_lock(POISON_LCM_F0_CV.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_factor0: fixture CV no longer declares Factor0Lock — the curve far-end guard cannot fire on it and its row would prove nothing")
ensure(scene_lcm_is_factor0_lock(POISON_LCM_F0_DSA.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_factor0: fixture DSA no longer declares Factor0Lock — the plane-A deform guard cannot fire on it and its row would prove nothing")
ensure(scene_lcm_is_factor0_lock(POISON_LCM_F0_DSB.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_factor0: fixture DSB no longer declares Factor0Lock — the plane-B deform guard cannot fire on it and its row would prove nothing")
ensure(scene_lcm_is_factor0_lock(POISON_LCM_F0_DR.sc_left_col_mask) == 1,
       "poison_scene_lcm_factor0: fixture DR no longer declares Factor0Lock — the drift guard cannot fire on it and its row would prove nothing")
